Explore how hosts, web properties, and certificates have changed over time.               
                                                                                          
Returns timeline events for hosts, observation ranges for certificates, and daily         
snapshots for web properties, within the specified time window.                           
                                                                                          
For web properties, --mode events returns scan timeline events instead of daily snapshots.
It requires web property event history to be enabled for your organization.               
                                                                                          
Web property history consumes credits, and longer windows cost more.                      
                                                                                          
To retrieve certificate history, you must have access to the Threat Hunting module.       

Usage:
  censys history <asset> [flags]

Examples:
  censys history 8.8.8.8 --start 2025-01-01T00:00:00Z --duration 30d
  censys history example.com:443 --end 2025-05-31T00:00:00Z --duration 72d
  censys history 56a06a23... --start 2025-01-01T00:00:00Z --end 2025-01-31T00:00:00Z
  censys history example.com:443 --duration 7d
  censys history example.com:443 --mode events --duration 30d
  censys history 8.8.8.8 --duration 14d

Flags:
  -d, --duration string   time window (e.g., 1d, 1w, 1y, 2h). Defaults to 7d (default "168h0m0s")
  -e, --end string        end time
  -h, --help              help for history
      --mode string       web property history source: snapshots (one lookup per day) or events (scan timeline) (default "snapshots")
  -o, --org-id string     organization ID to target (personal access tokens only)
  -s, --start string      start time

Global Flags:
      --debug                   enable debug logging
      --no-color                disable ANSI colors and styles
      --no-spinner              disable spinner during operations
  -O, --output-format string    output format (json|yaml|tree|short|template) (default "json")
  -q, --quiet                   suppress non-essential output
  -S, --streaming               enable streaming output mode (NDJSON) for commands that support it
      --timeout-http duration   per-request timeout for HTTP requests (e.g. 10s, 1m) - use 0 to disable

